  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Whole Carboniferous juvenile individual, likely developmental stage3 per2021 paper, not adult and not isolated shell. Anchor YPM IP168040 MazonCreek Moscovian, with same-species published restoration for damaged edges. {\"units\": \"meters\", \"prosoma_length_published\": 0.0069, \"prosoma_width_published\": 0.0168, \"opisthosoma_length_published\": 0.0073, \"opisthosoma_width_published\": 0.0112, \"telson_length_published\": 0.0079, \"body_plus_tail_sum\": 0.0221, \"shell_height_inferred\": 0.003, \"note\": \"2021Results explicit specimen dimensions authoritative. Figure1A caption2mm bar appears inconsistent with approximate width ratio; do not claim ruler and text agree or silently rescale.22.1mm sum is nominal anterior-posterior construction before overlap, not separately measured total.\"} Actual dorsal YPM IP168040 supplies outline and published dimensions;2021Fig1C is interpreted same-species reconstruction for poorly preserved spine margins, not a second measured specimen. 2020Fig19E-G YPM IP28514 shows real same-species ventral appendages; used only jointed organization, not dimensions or claimed same individual. CNS nerves indicate chelicera/fourwalking/pushing arrangement in2021discussion; actual ventral fine tips, shellheight, smallmouthparts, stance/color inferred conservatively. Do not use Limulus juvenile panelE as Euproops fossil, and do not substitute Piesberg Euproops sp adult flange morphology for this juvenile.",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Whole Carboniferous juvenile individual, likely developmental stage3 per2021 paper, not adult and not isolated shell. Anchor YPM IP168040 MazonCreek Moscovian, with same-species published restoration for damaged edges. {\"units\": \"meters\", \"prosoma_length_published\": 0.0069, \"prosoma_width_published\": 0.0168, \"opisthosoma_length_published\": 0.0073, \"opisthosoma_width_published\": 0.0112, \"telson_length_published\": 0.0079, \"body_plus_tail_sum\": 0.0221, \"shell_height_inferred\": 0.003, \"note\": \"2021Results explicit specimen dimensions authoritative. Figure1A caption2mm bar appears inconsistent with approximate width ratio; do not claim ruler and text agree or silently rescale.22.1mm sum is nominal anterior-posterior construction before overlap, not separately measured total.\"} Actual dorsal YPM IP168040 supplies outline and published dimensions;2021Fig1C is interpreted same-species reconstruction for poorly preserved spine margins, not a second measured specimen. 2020Fig19E-G YPM IP28514 shows real same-species ventral appendages; used only jointed organization, not dimensions or claimed same individual. CNS nerves indicate chelicera/fourwalking/pushing arrangement in2021discussion; actual ventral fine tips, shellheight, smallmouthparts, stance/color inferred conservatively. Do not use Limulus juvenile panelE as Euproops fossil, and do not substitute Piesberg Euproops sp adult flange morphology for this juvenile."
  },
